# API Endpoints

The backend runs on:

```text
http://localhost:5000
```

All endpoints return JSON responses.

## `GET /`

Checks whether the backend is running.

### Request

```bash
curl http://localhost:5000/
```

### Response

```json
{
  "status": "ok"
}
```

## `GET /api/projects`

Returns all projects from `projects.json`.

### Request

```bash
curl http://localhost:5000/api/projects
```

### Response

```json
[
  {
    "id": "mechx-website",
    "title": "MECHX Website",
    "description": "A website made for the Formula Student team.",
    "techStack": "HTML, CSS",
    "image": "",
    "link": "https://example.com/mechx"
  }
]
```

## `GET /api/projects/:id`

Returns a project using its ID.

### Request

```bash
curl http://localhost:5000/api/projects/mechx-website
```

### Response

```json
{
  "id": "mechx-website",
  "title": "MECHX Website",
  "description": "A website made for the Formula Student team.",
  "techStack": "HTML, CSS",
  "image": "",
  "link": "https://example.com/mechx"
}
```

If the project is not found:

```json
{
  "error": "Project not found"
}
```

HTTP status: `404`

## `POST /api/contact`

Submits a contact form message.

### Request

```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:5000/api/contact ^
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" ^
  -d "{\"name\":\"Ada\",\"email\":\"ada@example.com\",\"message\":\"Hello\"}"
```

### Response

HTTP status: `201`

```json
{
  "message": "Message submitted successfully.",
  "submission": {
    "name": "Ada",
    "email": "ada@example.com",
    "message": "Hello"
  }
}
```

If required fields are missing:

```json
{
  "error": "Name, email, and message are required."
}
```

HTTP status: `400`

If the email is invalid:

```json
{
  "error": "Please enter a valid email address."
}
```

HTTP status: `400`

## `GET /api/contact`

Returns contact submissions received since the backend started.

### Request

```bash
curl http://localhost:5000/api/contact
```

### Response

```json
[
  {
    "name": "Ada",
    "email": "ada@example.com",
    "message": "Hello"
  }
]
```

## Undefined Routes

Unknown routes return a JSON `404` response.

### Request

```bash
curl http://localhost:5000/api/doesnotexist
```

### Response

```json
{
  "error": "Route not found"
}
```

## Data Storage

* Project data is stored in `projects.json`.
* Contact submissions are stored temporarily in memory.
* Contact submissions are cleared when the backend restarts.
* No database is used.
